      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The **Guarded Write Journal** page (from [[write-journal]]) describes how the guarded write path implements transaction-like semantics for file operations:\n\n**Key points:**\n\n1. **Before-state Recording**: Before overwriting any file, the system records its prior state (the previous content if it existed, or a note that it didn\u0027t exist) into an in-memory write journal.\n\n2. **Rollback on Failure**: If the agent run fails for any reason\u2014turn cap exceeded, unrecoverable error, or denied writes\u2014the journal can roll back every recorded write in reverse order. This restores previous content to files that existed or deletes newly created files.\n\n3. **All-or-Nothing Semantics**: This approach gives each run all-or-nothing (atomic) semantics for its writes without requiring a database transaction. The journal itself serves as the transaction log, held in process memory for the duration of a single run.\n\n4. **Query Agent Exemption**: The Query agent never uses the journal\u0027s rollback path because it has no write tool at all\u2014the journal type exists in the shared agent runtime library but is only populated by agents that actually write.",
      "input_tokens": 5587,
      "output_tokens": 258
